Notes for regulators and reviewers:
- Variable selection: stepwise (BIC default) to prefer parsimony; final pruning via VIF ≤ 10 to mitigate multicollinearity
- Data handling: median imputation, optional log for skewed positive variables, winsorization at 1%/99%, standardization; all parameters are learned on train data only
- OLS assumptions: Jarque–Bera for normality, Breusch–Pagan for heteroscedasticity (if present, HC3 robust covariance is used for inference), Cook’s distance flagged but not auto-removed (explicit governance)
- Logistic assumptions: checks linearity of the logit (Box–Tidwell-like), separation handled conservatively (drop offending variables if encountered), VIF for multicollinearity
- Metrics: OLS reports RMSE/MAE/R2 (test and train), AIC/BIC and adj-R2 in-sample. Logistic reports AUC, KS, Brier score, log loss, optimal threshold by Youden’s J, confusion metrics, and calibration (intercept, slope)
- Transparency: no black-box regularization or complex transformations unless justified (optional simple log of skewed positive variables). All selections, bounds, and transformations reported in the output dict.

